From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:19:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/46] Flash Next: block-FP8 routed experts load a rank's
 whole experts and serve at --tp 2

Qwen's FP8 release converts only the routed experts (E4M3 weights, BF16 128x128
weight_scale_inv); shared-expert, attention and dense projections stay BF16. The
config check now names that layout as its own mode, the FP8 expert loader takes a
rank's experts in place of refusing world != 1, moe_native.fp8 takes its expert
count and shared slot from the rank's layer, and rank memory counts FP8 experts.

Device test flashnext-fp8-experts checks each rank's half against the one-GPU
bytes. Host tests match the base (one pre-existing rank-start crash).
